---
import InfoPage from "../components/InfoPage.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const GITHUB = site.repositoryUrl;
---

<InfoPage
  title="Transparency — mitlist"
  description="How mitlist plans to keep official hosting free, what it costs, and which promises do not change."
  eyebrow="Show the workings"
  heading="Free should come with a plan."
  intro="Official hosting is designed to stay modest, legible, and inexpensive to operate. This page records the limits, infrastructure, and funding model in public."
>
  <section class="info-card">
    <h2>What does not change</h2>
    <div>
      <ul>
        <li>The complete self-hosted product stays free and open source under the AGPL.</li>
        <li>There will be no ads and no selling household data.</li>
        <li>The official app will not deliberately cripple self-hosting.</li>
        <li>Export and account deletion remain available; your data is not leverage.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="info-card">
    <h2>How hosting stays small</h2>
    <div>
      <p>The hosted service runs across infrastructure we operate in Eygelshoven, the Netherlands, and Nuremberg, Germany. PostgreSQL is self-managed and replicated, Cloudflare fronts the service, and Cloudflare R2 stores attachments under our EU data-location configuration. Each household has 1 GB of file storage, with atomic quota reservations and cleanup of abandoned uploads.</p>
      <p>Mobile list recognition runs on iOS and Android devices. No hosted AI service is called for a scan.</p>
      <p>Encrypted PostgreSQL backups are taken twice daily. A rolling 30-day retention policy and a separate recovery copy for R2 attachments are public-beta launch work; until those controls are verified, we do not claim a zero recovery point or independent attachment backup.</p>
      <p>Other services in the loop: Amazon SES in Frankfurt for transactional email, Firebase for push notifications and app attestation, Cloudflare Turnstile for guest sign-up on the web, and a self-run GlitchTip for crash reports. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> lists each one with what it receives.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="info-card">
    <h2>How the money works</h2>
    <div>
      <p>Households of up to four members use official hosting for free. Households of five or more people pay €3.99 monthly or €29.99 yearly for Premium. One subscription covers the household and unlocks nothing else: no feature gates, no ads, no upsells. Web subscriptions run through Polar; in-app subscriptions through the App Store and Google Play. Taxes and the final amount are shown before payment, and store prices may vary by region.</p>
      <p>Premium pays for infrastructure first. As the hosted service settles, this page will publish the monthly compute, storage, email, and monitoring totals rather than inventing numbers in advance.</p>
      <p>If Premium cannot cover growth, the first response is tighter fair-use limits, announced here at least 30 days ahead — not feature locks in the open-source app.</p>
      <div class="info-actions"><a class="btn" href={GITHUB} rel="noopener">Follow the work on GitHub</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</InfoPage>
